# TypeScript + TDD (GoodPlays web)

## Red → Green → Refactor

Colocate tests: `feature.ts` + `feature.test.ts` in `apps/web/src/`.

```bash
cd apps/web && npm test
```

## Stack

- React 19, Vite, TanStack Query, Clerk
- API client in `apps/web/src/lib/api.ts` (or equivalent)
- Env: `VITE_API_URL`, `VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, `VITE_BASE_PATH`

## Rules

- Extract testable logic from components into `lib/` hooks and utils
- Mock `fetch` or API module in unit tests — no real API in unit layer
- Strict TypeScript; no `any` without comment

## Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ Typed API response
type LibraryEntry = { id: string; gameId: string; status: string; rating?: number };

// ✅ Query key factory
const libraryKeys = { all: ['library'] as const, list: () => [...libraryKeys.all, 'list'] as const };
```

## Avoid

- IGDB or LLM calls from browser
- Storing secrets in frontend env beyond Clerk publishable key
- Business rules buried in JSX event handlers

## Agents

- UI features → `/website-developer`
- E2E → `/website-tester`
- Backend endpoints → `/tdd`
